ove is (g = 10 m/s², √3 = 1.73)","138.4 m","160 m","80 m","69.2 m","R = u² sin 2θ / g = 1600 × (√3/2) / 10 = 160 × 0.865 = 138.4 m."],["Physics","","A 2 kg mass is attached to a string and whirled in a vertical circle of radius 0.5 m. The minimum speed at the top for the string to stay taut is (g = 10 m/s²)","√5 m/s","5 m/s","√10 m/s","2.5 m/s","At the top mg = mv²/r, so v² = gr = 5 and v = √5 m/s."],["Physics","","A satellite of mass 500 kg orbits at a height where g = 2.5 m/s². Its weight there is","1 250 N","5 000 N","200 N","12 500 N","W = mg = 500 × 2.5 = 1 250 N."],["Physics","","A uniform ladder of weight 200 N and length 5 m leans against a smooth wall at 4 m height. The friction needed at the ground is","75 N","100 N","150 N","50 N","Base is 3 m from the wall. Torque about the base: R × 4 = 200 × 1.5, so R = 75 N and friction equals R = 75 N."],["Physics","","A 0.4 kg ball moving at 5 m/s collides head-on with a stationary 0.6 kg ball and they stick together. The loss of kinetic energy is","3 J","5 J","2 J","1 J","v = 0.4×5/1.0 = 2 m/s. KE before = ½×0.4×25 = 5 J; after = ½×1.0×4 = 2 J; loss = 3 J."],["Physics","","A machine delivers 1 200 J of work in 40 s with an efficiency of 75%. The input power is","40 W","30 W","1 600 W","900 W","Output power = 30 W; input = 30/0.75 = 40 W."],["Physics","","A pendulum clock with a simple pendulum of length 1 m has a period of 2 s. If the length is made 0.25 m, the period becomes","1 s","0.5 s","4 s","2 s","T ∝ √L. √0.25 = 0.5, so T = 1 s."],["Physics","","A mass of 0.1 kg oscillates on a spring with amplitude 0.05 m and angular frequency 20 rad/s. The maximum speed is","1 m/s","0.5 m/s","2 m/s","0.25 m/s","v_max = Aω = 0.05 × 20 = 1 m/s."],["Physics","","What mass of ice at 0 °C is melted by 1.68 × 10⁵ J of heat? (L = 3.36 × 10⁵ J/kg)","0.5 kg","2 kg","0.25 kg","1 kg","m = Q/L = 1.68 × 10⁵ / 3.36 × 10⁵ = 0.5 kg."],["Physics","","200 g of water at 80 °C is mixed with 300 g of water at 20 °C. Ignoring heat loss, the final temperature is","44 °C","50 °C","56 °C","40 °C","200(80 − T) = 300(T − 20) → 16 000 − 200T = 300T − 6 000 → T = 44 °C."],["Physics","","A copper block of mass 0.5 kg at 100 °C is dropped into 1 kg of water at 20 °C. The final temperature is (c copper = 400 J/kg K, c water = 4 200 J/kg K, ignore losses; to nearest °C)","24 °C","30 °C","100 °C","60 °C","0.5×400×(100 − T) = 1×4200×(T − 20) → 20 000 − 200T = 4 200T − 84 000 → T = 104 000/4 400 = 23.6 °C ≈ 24 °C."],["Physics","","A gas expands from 2 dm³ to 5 dm³ at a constant pressure of 2 × 10⁵ Pa. The work done by the gas is","600 J","400 J","1 000 J","200 J","W = PΔV = 2 × 10⁵ × 3 × 10⁻³ = 600 J."],["Physics","","At what temperature will the volume of a gas, initially 300 cm³ at 27 °C, become 400 cm³ at constant pressure?","127 °C","36 °C","400 °C","67 °C","V/T constant: 400/300 × 300 K = 400 K = 127 °C."],["Physics","","A concave mirror of focal length 20 cm forms a real image 60 cm from the mirror. The object distance is","30 cm","15 cm","80 cm","40 cm","1/u = 1/20 − 1/60 = 2/60, so u = 30 cm."],["Physics","","A converging lens gives a virtual image three times the size of the object at 20 cm from the lens. The focal length is","10 cm","30 cm","15 cm","60 cm","The virtual image is at v = −20 cm and m = 3, so u = 20/3 cm. 1/f = 1/u + 1/v = 3/20 − 1/20 = 1/10, so f = 10 cm."],["Physics","","Light of wavelength 600 nm falls on a diffraction grating with 5 000 lines per cm. The angle of the first-order maximum satisfies sin θ =","0.3","0.6","0.03","3.0","d = 1/5000 cm = 2 × 10⁻⁶ m; sin θ = λ/d = 6 × 10⁻⁷ / 2 × 10⁻⁶ = 0.3."],["Physics","","In Young’s experiment the slit separation is 0.5 mm, the screen is 2 m away and the fringe spacing is 2 mm. The wavelength is","500 nm","400 nm","1 000 nm","250 nm","λ = xd/D = 2×10⁻³ × 0.5×10⁻³ / 2 = 5 × 10⁻⁷ m = 500 nm."],["Physics","","A string of length 1.2 m fixed at both ends vibrates in its second harmonic at 100 Hz. The wave speed is","120 m/s","60 m/s","240 m/s","100 m/s","λ = L = 1.2 m for the 2nd harmonic. v = fλ = 120 m/s."],["Physics","","A source of frequency 500 Hz moves towards a stationary observer at 20 m/s. The speed of sound is 340 m/s. The observed frequency is","531 Hz","469 Hz","500 Hz","520 Hz","f' = f v/(v − vs) = 500 × 340/320 = 531.25 Hz."],["Physics","","Three 6 Ω resistors are connected so that two are in parallel and this pair is in series with the third. The total resistance is","9 Ω","12 Ω","4 Ω","18 Ω","Pair = 3 Ω; plus 6 Ω = 9 Ω."],["Physics","","A cell of e.m.f. 12 V and internal resistance 2 Ω is connected to a 4 Ω resistor. The terminal p.d. is","8 V","12 V","6 V","4 V","I = 12/6 = 2 A; V = IR = 2 × 4 = 8 V."],["Physics","","A 60 W lamp is used for 8 hours a day for 30 days. At ₦70 per kWh, the cost is","₦1 008","₦504","₦2 016","₦100.8","Energy = 0.06 × 240 = 14.4 kWh; 14.4 × 70 = ₦1 008."],["Physics","","A capacitor of 20 μF is charged to 50 V. The energy stored is","25 mJ","50 mJ","10 mJ","1 J","E = ½CV² = ½ × 20×10⁻⁶ × 2500 = 0.025 J = 25 mJ."],["Physics","","A coil of inductance 0.2 H has the current in it changing at 50 A/s. The induced e.m.f. is","10 V","250 V","0.004 V","100 V","E = L dI/dt = 0.2 × 50 = 10 V."],["Physics","","An alternating voltage V = 200 sin 100πt is applied across a resistor. The frequency is","50 Hz","100 Hz","200 Hz","314 Hz","ω = 100π so f = ω/2π = 50 Hz."],["Physics","","A transformer with 500 primary turns and 50 secondary turns is connected to a 220 V a.c. supply. The output voltage is","22 V","2 200 V","220 V","11 V","Vs = 220 × 50/500 = 22 V."],["Physics","","A wire carries 5 A in a magnetic field of 0.4 T. The force per metre of the wire (perpendicular) is","2 N/m","0.8 N/m","20 N/m","1.25 N/m","F/L = BI = 0.4 × 5 = 2 N/m."],["Physics","","An electron moves at 2 × 10⁶ m/s perpendicular to a magnetic field of 0.01 T. The force is (e = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C)","3.2 × 10⁻¹⁵ N","1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ N","3.2 × 10⁻¹⁷ N","8 × 10⁻²⁶ N","F = Bev = 0.01 × 1.6×10⁻¹⁹ × 2×10⁶ = 3.2 × 10⁻¹⁵ N."],["Physics","","The energy of a photon of frequency 5 × 10¹⁴ Hz is (h = 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ J s)","3.3 × 10⁻¹⁹ J","1.3 × 10⁻²⁰ J","6.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J","3.3 × 10⁻³⁴ J","E = hf = 6.6×10⁻³⁴ × 5×10¹⁴ = 3.3 × 10⁻¹⁹ J."],["Physics","","The work function of a metal is 3.0 eV. The longest wavelength that causes photoemission is (hc = 1240 eV nm)","413 nm","300 nm","1 240 nm","3 720 nm","λ = hc/φ = 1240/3 ≈ 413 nm."],["Physics","","A radioactive sample has an initial activity of 640 Bq and a half-life of 5 hours. After 20 hours its activity is","40 Bq","80 Bq","160 Bq","20 Bq","20 h = 4 half-lives: 640/16 = 40 Bq."],["Physics","","The mass defect of a nucleus is 0.03 u. The binding energy is (1 u = 931 MeV)","27.9 MeV","0.03 MeV","931 MeV","2.79 MeV","E = 0.03 × 931 = 27.93 MeV."],["Physics","","In the reaction ²³⁵₉₂U + n → ¹⁴¹₅₆Ba + ⁹²₃₆Kr + x n, the value of x is","3","2","1","4","Mass number: 235 + 1 = 141 + 92 + x, so x = 3."],["Physics","","A body of mass 5 kg is pulled up a rough slope of 30° by a force of 40 N parallel to the slope. The friction force is 5 N. The acceleration is (g = 10 m/s²)","2 m/s²","4 m/s²","1.8 m/s²","8 m/s²","Net force = 40 − 5 − 5×10×0.5 = 10 N; a = 10/5 = 2 m/s²."],["Physics","","A car of mass 1 000 kg travels round a circular bend of radius 50 m at 10 m/s. The friction force needed is","2 000 N","200 N","500 N","1 000 N","F = mv²/r = 1000 × 100/50 = 2 000 N."],["Physics","","The pressure of a gas of density 1.2 kg/m³ whose molecules have mean square speed 90 000 m²/s² is (P = ⅓ρc²)","36 000 Pa","108 000 Pa","12 000 Pa","90 000 Pa","P = ⅓ × 1.2 × 90 000 = 36 000 Pa."],["Physics","","A uniform wire of resistance 12 Ω is bent to form a circle. The resistance between two points at opposite ends of a diameter is","3 Ω","6 Ω","12 Ω","24 Ω","Two 6 Ω halves in parallel: 3 Ω."],["Physics","","A 100 μF capacitor discharges through a 10 kΩ resistor. The time constant is","1 s","10 s","0.01 s","100 s","τ = RC = 10⁴ × 10⁻⁴ = 1 s."],["Physics","","The potential difference needed to accelerate an electron from rest to a speed of 4 × 10⁶ m/s is (m = 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ kg, e = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C)","45.5 V","91 V","22.8 V","4.55 V","eV = ½mv²: V = 9.1×10⁻³¹ × 1.6×10¹³ /(2 × 1.6×10⁻¹⁹) = 45.5 V."],["Chemistry","","What mass of NaCl is needed to prepare 250 cm³ of a 0.4 mol dm⁻³ solution? (Na = 23, Cl = 35.5)","5.85 g","23.4 g","11.7 g","1.46 g","n = 0.4 × 0.25 = 0.1 mol; mass = 0.1 × 58.5 = 5.85 g."],["Chemistry","","25.0 cm³ of 0.20 mol dm⁻³ HCl is neutralised by 20.0 cm³ of Ba(OH)₂ solution. The concentration of the Ba(OH)₂ is","0.125 mol dm⁻³","0.25 mol dm⁻³","0.5 mol dm⁻³","0.0625 mol dm⁻³","n(HCl) = 0.005 mol; Ba(OH)₂ + 2HCl, so n = 0.0025 mol in 0.020 dm³ = 0.125 mol dm⁻³."],["Chemistry","","In 1 mol of calcium phosphate, Ca₃(PO₄)₂, the number of moles of oxygen atoms is","8","4","2","3","Each PO₄ has 4 O and there are 2 PO₄ groups: 8 mol."],["Chemistry","","The mass of oxygen in 31 g of calcium phosphate is nearest to (Ca₃(PO₄)₂ = 310; O = 16)","12.8 g","6.4 g","3.2 g","31 g","31 g is 0.1 mol of Ca₃(PO₄)₂, which contains 0.8 mol O = 12.8 g."],["Chemistry","","5.6 dm³ of a gas at s.t.p. has a mass of 7 g. The relative molecular mass is","28","14","56","7","n = 0.25 mol; M = 7/0.25 = 28."],["Chemistry","","A hydrocarbon of molar mass 78 g/mol contains 92.3% carbon. Its molecular formula is (C = 12, H = 1)","C₆H₆","C₂H₂","C₄H₄","C₆H₁₂","C: 78 × 0.923 = 72 g = 6 atoms; H: 6 atoms."],["Chemistry","","The volume of 0.5 mol dm⁻³ H₂SO₄ that will react completely with 2.0 g of NaOH is (Na = 23, O = 16, H = 1)","50 cm³","100 cm³","25 cm³","200 cm³","n(NaOH) = 0.05 mol → 0.025 mol H₂SO₄ → 0.025/0.5 = 0.05 dm³ = 50 cm³."],["Chemistry","","When 1.0 g of magnesium ribbon burns, 1.67 g of magnesium oxide forms. The oxygen combined is","0.67 g","1.00 g","0.33 g","2.67 g","1.67 − 1.00 = 0.67 g of oxygen."],["Chemistry","","Calculate the pH of a solution made by diluting 10 cm³ of 0.1 mol dm⁻³ HCl to 1 dm³.","3","1","2","4","c = 0.001 mol dm⁻³ so pH = 3."],["Chemistry","","A weak acid HA (0.1 mol dm⁻³) has Kₐ = 1.0 × 10⁻⁷. Its pH is","4","7","1","3.5","[H⁺] = √(Ka c) = √(10⁻⁸) = 10⁻⁴, pH = 4."],["Chemistry","","The solubility of Mg(OH)₂ is 1.0 × 10⁻⁴ mol dm⁻³. Its solubility product is","4 × 10⁻¹²","1 × 10⁻⁸","4 × 10⁻⁸","1 × 10⁻¹²","[Mg²⁺] = 10⁻⁴, [OH⁻] = 2 × 10⁻⁴; Ksp = 10⁻⁴ × 4 × 10⁻⁸ = 4 × 10⁻¹²."],["Chemistry","","For N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃, at equilibrium [N₂] = 1.0, [H₂] = 2.0 and [NH₃] = 4.0 mol dm⁻³. Kc is","2.0 mol⁻² dm⁶","0.5 mol⁻² dm⁶","8.0 mol⁻² dm⁶","16 mol⁻² dm⁶","Kc = [NH₃]²/([N₂][H₂]³) = 16/(1 × 8) = 2.0."],["Chemistry","","For H₂ + I₂ ⇌ 2HI, 1 mol of H₂ and 1 mol of I₂ in a 1 dm³ vessel reach equilibrium with 1.6 mol of HI. Kc is","64","16","4","2.56","[HI] = 1.6, so [H₂] = [I₂] = 1 − 0.8 = 0.2. Kc = 1.6²/(0.2 × 0.2) = 2.56/0.04 = 64."],["Chemistry","","The reaction A → B has a rate constant 0.02 s⁻¹ and is first order. The half-life is (ln 2 = 0.693)","34.7 s","0.014 s","69.3 s","17.3 s","t½ = 0.693/k = 0.693/0.02 = 34.65 s."],["Chemistry","","The initial rate of a reaction doubles when [A] is doubled and quadruples when [B] is doubled. The rate law is","rate = k[A][B]²","rate = k[A]²[B]","rate = k[A][B]","rate = k[A]²[B]²","First order in A (2×) and second order in B (4×)."],["Chemistry","","The enthalpy change of formation of CO₂(g) is −394 kJ mol⁻¹ and of CO(g) is −111 kJ mol⁻¹. ΔH for CO + ½O₂ → CO₂ is","−283 kJ mol⁻¹","−505 kJ mol⁻¹","+283 kJ mol⁻¹","−111 kJ mol⁻¹","ΔH = −394 − (−111) = −283 kJ mol⁻¹."],["Chemistry","","Burning 0.5 g of a fuel raises the temperature of 200 g of water by 10 °C. (c = 4.2 J g⁻¹ K⁻¹.) The heat evolved per gram of fuel is","16.8 kJ","8.4 kJ","4.2 kJ","33.6 kJ","Q = 200 × 4.2 × 10 = 8 400 J for 0.5 g, so 16 800 J/g = 16.8 kJ/g."],["Chemistry","","In the electrolysis of aqueous CuSO₄ using a current of 5 A for 965 s, the mass of copper deposited is (Cu = 64, F = 96 500 C)","1.6 g","3.2 g","0.8 g","6.4 g","Q = 4 825 C; n(e⁻) = 0.05 mol; n(Cu) = 0.025 mol; mass = 1.6 g."],["Chemistry"