 methanoate","ethane","Alkaline hydrolysis gives the salt of the acid."],["Chemistry","","How many σ bonds are in a molecule of ethene?","5","6","4","2","C–H ×4, C–C σ ×1 = 5 σ bonds (and one π)."],["Chemistry","","The shape of the SF₆ molecule is","octahedral","tetrahedral","trigonal bipyramidal","square planar","Six bonding pairs around S give octahedral geometry."],["Chemistry","","Which of the following has the highest boiling point?","CH₃CH₂CH₂OH","CH₃CH₂CH₃","CH₃OCH₃","CH₃CH₂CH₂CH₃","Hydrogen bonding in the alcohol raises its boiling point."],["Chemistry","","The metal extracted by electrolysis of its oxide dissolved in molten cryolite is","aluminium","iron","zinc","copper","Aluminium is obtained by the Hall–Héroult process."],["Chemistry","","In the Haber process, increasing the pressure","increases the yield of ammonia","decreases the yield","has no effect","lowers the rate","Four moles of gas become two; high pressure favours NH₃."],["Chemistry","","The reduction of copper(II) oxide by hydrogen is represented by CuO + H₂ → Cu + H₂O. The mass of copper formed from 4.0 g of CuO is (Cu = 64, O = 16)","3.2 g","6.4 g","1.6 g","4.0 g","n(CuO) = 4/80 = 0.05 mol; Cu = 0.05 × 64 = 3.2 g."],["Chemistry","","The percentage of water of crystallisation in CuSO₄·5H₂O is (Cu = 64, S = 32, O = 16, H = 1)","36%","64%","25%","50%","5H₂O = 90; M = 250; 90/250 = 36%."],["Chemistry","","A gas diffuses 2 times faster than oxygen. Its relative molecular mass is","8","16","64","32","Rate ∝ 1/√M: M = 32/4 = 8."],["Chemistry","","The volume of CO₂ at s.t.p. produced by burning 3.0 g of carbon completely is (C = 12; molar volume = 22.4 dm³)","5.6 dm³","11.2 dm³","2.8 dm³","22.4 dm³","n(C) = 0.25 mol gives 0.25 mol CO₂ = 5.6 dm³."],["Chemistry","","The number of chloride ions in 0.1 mol of MgCl₂ is (L = 6 × 10²³)","1.2 × 10²³","6 × 10²²","3.6 × 10²³","6 × 10²³","0.1 mol gives 0.2 mol Cl⁻ = 1.2 × 10²³ ions."],["Biology","","A heterozygous red-flowered plant (Rr, red dominant) is self-p